<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
  <PackageReference Include="FsCheck.Xunit" Version="2.16.6" />
  <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.11.1" />
  <PackageReference Include="Moq" Version="4.20.70" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.5.3" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="2.5.3" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Core\PhantomVault.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\Crypto\GiblexVault.Security.ZK.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
        Two settings, both about a suite whose cost is dominated by Argon2id (256 MiB, 6 ops
        per derivation, and the lifecycle tests derive repeatedly).

        maxParallelThreads caps memory, not CPU. xUnit defaults to one worker per core, and
        each concurrent collection can hold a 256 MiB KDF allocation: 4 GB of KDF alone on a
        16-core machine, and the Core suite was measured at 5 GB within a minute of starting.
        The host has aborted mid-run more than once. 8 is chosen so CI is untouched — a
        GitHub windows-latest runner has 4 cores and would never exceed it — while a
        high-core developer box stays bounded.

        Being straight about the evidence: a full run HAS completed clean at default
        parallelism (820 passed), and the highest figure measured, 10.3 GB, was inflated by
        other test runs happening at the same time. So this is a guard against a plausible and
        cheap-to-prevent failure, not a fix for a proven one. If it ever costs real time,
        raising it is defensible — deleting it without re-measuring is not.

        longRunningTestSeconds flags any single test past two minutes: in a ~37-minute run,
        a genuine hang would otherwise be invisible inside the expected slowness.

        The runner config only takes effect if it sits next to the test assembly.
    -->
    <None Include="xunit.runner.json" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
